<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guan Shu Xian</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Guan Shu Xian was the third son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/king-wen-of-zhou">King Wen of Zhou</a> and an elder brother of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duke-of-zhou">Duke of Zhou</a>. After the Zhou conquest of the Shang he was enfeoffed at Guan and, with his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cai-shu-du">Cai Shu Du</a> and Huo Shu, set to watch over the Shang heir <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wu-geng">Wu Geng</a>. When the Duke of Zhou became regent he joined Wu Geng in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rebellion-of-the-three-guards">Rebellion of the Three Guards</a> and was executed after its defeat.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guan-shu-xian.jpg" alt="Guan Shu Xian" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Digital file creation, see the contributor names shown in the “User” column of the “File history” section below. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E9%AE%AE-seal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
